THE ENTRIES-13/17 CHANNEL CHECK (repair14_20260916/FABLE_RULING_20260917.md B: "name the mutant each kills and the
observable that differs ... If a body-tested-partition mutant escapes -> L2, IN as the pair; if the count cannot vary
under any such mutant -> clause (e), disclosed.")
  THE CELL: ACCEPTS entries 13/17, `sw'/`sd +0x08 = 0x0200' (DOG_ENABLE alone).  In dev_sgi_ip32.c 8c1d1545: the width
    arm stores it (:275-295), but the prelude re-forces CONTROL = ENDIANESS at EVERY access (:231), so the stored value
    is visible to nothing.  The CONTROL arm tests DOG (:361) and clears it (:362), tests HARD_RESET (:364), clears
    ENDIANESS (:375) and prints iff the residue is nonzero (:377-379).  For 0x0200 the residue is 0: nothing prints and
    nothing stops.
  THE BODY-TESTED PARTITIONS the cell's value reaches: DOG set; HARD_RESET clear; residue 0.  One mutant per action:
    D_nodogclear  DOG's test kept, its clear deleted -> residue 0x200 -> the arm PRINTS.  OBSERVABLE: the count of
                  `CRIME_CONTROL: unimplemented' in a session holding an accepted 0x0200 write.  BUILT HERE.
    DOG -> stop   (e.g. the :364 test widened to DOG|HARD_RESET) -> the CPUs stop on 0x0200.  OBSERVABLE: the RAM
                  trip after it -- ALREADY READ by `rearm surv' and `latch surv', whose sessions run roundtrip(A)
                  after all 46 ACCEPTS entries, 13 and 17 among them.  Not built: a shipped row owns the channel.
    re-arm/pre-set in the DOG branch -> read by `rearm once', `latch x5', `latch said' (why 0x0200 is IN ACCEPTS).
  WHO READS D_nodogclear's OBSERVABLE TODAY: NO ROW.  Five rows count `CRIME_CONTROL: unimplemented' (grep -n in the
    probe): `sw08 msg ctl' (its session: sw 0x01), `sb08 msg' and `sh08b msg' (REFUSED narrow writes -- declined before
    the arm), `acc ctl sd' (sd 0x01), `p acc ctl msg' (sd 0x01, sw 0x0001, sw 0x0201, sd 0x0201).  None writes 0x0200.
    The 0x0201 writes print under both builds (residue 0x1 on the fix, 0x201 on the mutant: the count is unchanged).
    The ACCEPTS sessions, which DO write 0x0200, count only `-- declined.'.
  PREDICTION: D_nodogclear is GREEN on all 216 rows that are not the pair -- which, sessions being independent, IS its
    score against the probe without the pair: an escape -- and RED on exactly the pair.  GRADE, by the ruling's own
    conditional: L2, IN as the pair.  CONFIRMED only if the table shows exactly that.  If any other row reds, the cell
    was covered, the pair is NOT owed and leaves the diff, and this file's prediction is recorded as a miss.
  DISCLOSED, not rowed: a SILENT decline of the DOG-only write (no announce) is EQUIVALENT -- nothing any access can
    see changes; the latch x DOG joint is clause (e) -- the CONTROL arm reads no latch.
